  {
   "id": "intro",
   "type": "intro",
   "heading": {
    "en": "A ring or a scatter?",
    "kn": "ಉಂಗುರವೋ ಚದುರಿದವೋ?"
   },
   "hook": {
    "en": "Slice a sunflower stem and the vascular bundles form a neat ring. Slice a maize stem and they are scattered like dots. On a hot afternoon, why do some grass leaves roll up?",
    "kn": "ಸೂರ್ಯಕಾಂತಿ ಕಾಂಡದಲ್ಲಿ ನಾಳಪುಂಜಗಳು ಉಂಗುರದಂತೆ, ಮೆಕ್ಕೆಜೋಳದಲ್ಲಿ ಚುಕ್ಕೆಗಳಂತೆ ಚದುರಿವೆ. ಬಿಸಿಲಿನ ಮಧ್ಯಾಹ್ನ ಹುಲ್ಲಿನ ಎಲೆಗಳು ಏಕೆ ಸುರುಳಿಯಾಗುತ್ತವೆ?"
   },
   "objectives": [
    {
     "en": "Compare dicot and monocot stems"
    },
    {
     "en": "Compare dorsiventral and isobilateral leaves"
    },
    {
     "en": "Explain the role of bulliform cells"
    }
   ],
   "narration": {
    "en": "Slice a sunflower stem and the vascular bundles form a neat ring. Slice a maize stem and they are scattered like dots. On a hot afternoon, why do some grass leaves roll up?",
    "kn": "ಸೂರ್ಯಕಾಂತಿ ಕಾಂಡದಲ್ಲಿ ನಾಳಪುಂಜಗಳು ಉಂಗುರದಂತೆ, ಮೆಕ್ಕೆಜೋಳದಲ್ಲಿ ಚುಕ್ಕೆಗಳಂತೆ ಚದುರಿವೆ. ಬಿಸಿಲಿನ ಮಧ್ಯಾಹ್ನ ಹುಲ್ಲಿನ ಎಲೆಗಳು ಏಕೆ ಸುರುಳಿಯಾಗುತ್ತವೆ?"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "concept1",
   "type": "concept",
   "title": {
    "en": "Dicot stem"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "A young dicot stem has an epidermis with a cuticle, trichomes and a few stomata. The cortex has a collenchymatous hypodermis, parenchymatous cortical layers and an endodermis whose cells are rich in starch grains, so it is called the starch sheath. The pericycle forms semi-lunar patches of sclerenchyma above the phloem. The vascular bundles are arranged in a ring, which is characteristic of the dicot stem, and each is conjoint, open and endarch. Medullary rays lie between the bundles and a large pith occupies the centre.",
    "kn": "ದ್ವಿದಳ ಕಾಂಡದಲ್ಲಿ ಕೊಲೆಂಕೈಮಾ ಅಧಶ್ಚರ್ಮ, ಪಿಷ್ಟ ಕವಚ ಎನ್ನುವ ಅಂತಶ್ಚರ್ಮ, ಅರ್ಧಚಂದ್ರಾಕಾರದ ಸ್ಕ್ಲೀರೆಂಕೈಮಾ ಪರಿಚಕ್ರ. ನಾಳಪುಂಜಗಳು ಉಂಗುರದಲ್ಲಿ; ಸಂಯುಕ್ತ, ತೆರೆದ, ಎಂಡಾರ್ಕ್."
   },
   "points": [
    {
     "en": "Collenchymatous hypodermis"
    },
    {
     "en": "Endodermis = starch sheath"
    },
    {
     "en": "Ring of conjoint, open, endarch bundles"
    }
   ],
   "narration": {
    "en": "A young dicot stem has an epidermis with a cuticle, trichomes and a few stomata. The cortex has a collenchymatous hypodermis, parenchymatous cortical layers and an endodermis whose cells are rich in starch grains, so it is called the starch sheath. The pericycle forms semi-lunar patches of sclerenchyma above the phloem.",
    "kn": "ದ್ವಿದಳ ಕಾಂಡದಲ್ಲಿ ಕೊಲೆಂಕೈಮಾ ಅಧಶ್ಚರ್ಮ, ಪಿಷ್ಟ ಕವಚ ಎನ್ನುವ ಅಂತಶ್ಚರ್ಮ, ಅರ್ಧಚಂದ್ರಾಕಾರದ ಸ್ಕ್ಲೀರೆಂಕೈಮಾ ಪರಿಚಕ್ರ. ನಾಳಪುಂಜಗಳು ಉಂಗುರದಲ್ಲಿ; ಸಂಯುಕ್ತ, ತೆರೆದ, ಎಂಡಾರ್ಕ್."
   }
